{"name":"Rhodonite","hex":"#f3b3c5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rhodonite","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A manganese inosilicate mineral with some substitution by iron and magnesium, of composition (Mn,Fe,Mg,Ca)SiO3."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rhodonite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rhodonite","blocks":[{"text":"Rhodonite is a manganese inosilicate, with the formula (Mn, Fe, Mg, Ca)SiO3, and member of the pyroxenoid group of minerals, crystallizing in the triclinic system. The term rhodonite was first introduced by Germar. from Ancient Greek  ῥόδον (rhódon) 'rose'. It commonly occurs as cleavable to compact masses with a rose-red color often tending to brown due to surface oxidation. The rose-red hue is caused by the manganese cation (Mn2+)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/8224M-rhodonite3.jpg/330px-8224M-rhodonite3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhodonite"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Rhodonite09.jpg/500px-Rhodonite09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Rhodonite09.jpg/500px-Rhodonite09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pink rhodonite contrasting with black manganese oxides is sometimes used as gemstone material as seen in this specimen from Humboldt County, Nevada.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARhodonite09.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Tomb_of_Tsarina_Maria_Alexandrovna%2C_wife%2C_of_Tsar_Alexander_II%2C_Peter_and_Paul_Cathedral_%2837185567485%29.jpg/500px-Tomb_of_Tsarina_Maria_Alexandrovna%2C_wife%2C_of_Tsar_Alexander_II%2C_Peter_and_Paul_Cathedral_%2837185567485%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Tomb_of_Tsarina_Maria_Alexandrovna%2C_wife%2C_of_Tsar_Alexander_II%2C_Peter_and_Paul_Cathedral_%2837185567485%29.jpg/1280px-Tomb_of_Tsarina_Maria_Alexandrovna%2C_wife%2C_of_Tsar_Alexander_II%2C_Peter_and_Paul_Cathedral_%2837185567485%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Tomb_of_Tsarina_Maria_Alexandrovna%2C_wife%2C_of_Tsar_Alexander_II%2C_Peter_and_Paul_Cathedral_%2837185567485%29.jpg/500px-Tomb_of_Tsarina_Maria_Alexandrovna%2C_wife%2C_of_Tsar_Alexander_II%2C_Peter_and_Paul_Cathedral_%2837185567485%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tomb of Tsarina Maria Alexandrovna, wife, of Tsar Alexander II, Peter and Paul Cathedral","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATomb_of_Tsarina_Maria_Alexandrovna%2C_wife%2C_of_Tsar_Alexander_II%2C_Peter_and_Paul_Cathedral_(37185567485).jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}